From: WokeNet Maintainers <security@woke.social>
Subject: [PATCH] Fail closed for WokeNet live-cluster safety

Unknown custom genesis hashes are classified as non-live upstream, which
skips production identity, sandbox, multiprocess, benchmark, workspace, and
stack protections. Require the explicit downstream WokeNet safety mode for
every unknown non-local production cluster, bind it to the configured exact
genesis hash, and fail closed unless it uses fully native Firedancer with
every existing live-cluster safeguard.

Preserve upstream classification only for local/development or recognized
built-in clusters, reject built-in Solana and Pyth hashes in WokeNet mode,
and exercise the parser, classification, and every policy branch in the
native config test.

